<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang="en-US">OBDMID</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang="en-US">The OBDMIDs $00, $20, $40, $60, $80, $A0, $C0, $E0 result in an response that contains the supported OBDMIDs in the respective range. (e.g. $40 -&gt; response describes the PIDs in range $41-$60.
Note, in this case one OBDMID is mandatory and at most 6 OBDMIDs are allowed.
Each other OBDMID results in a response that contains the corresponding OBDMID data (e.g. $03 -&gt; response contains info about Oxygen Sensor Monitor Bank1-Sensor3).
Note, in this case exactly 1 OBDMID is required/allowed.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>OBDMID</QUAL>
</STATICCOMP>
</REQ>
