</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang="en-US">The pupose of this service is to provide access to the results for on-board diagnostic monitoring tests of specific components/systems that are continously monitored (e.g. mis-fire monitoring) and non-continously monitored (e.g. catalyst systems).</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>_06_RequestOnboardMonitoringTestResult_ReadSupportedOBDMID</QUAL>
<REQ oid="6088DB8D1A9D4061B602EFEEE3325AA8" temploid="9BB7D0DDEDE34ebf96366626FC603432">
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang="en-US">Request</TUV>
</NAME>
<QUAL>Req</QUAL>
<CONSTCOMP id="_000001FECAA9FB20" oid="6E02E0492A2C40988E6CC895F6B4C135" temploid="26C34875006247219CE003F023E439ED" must="1" spec="sid" bl="8" v="6">
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang="en-US">SID-RQ</TUV>
</NAME>
<QUAL>SID_RQ</QUAL>
</CONSTCOMP>
<STATICCOMP id="_000001FECAAB7F00" oid="A91D070588994b0bAAF76A4B931349CC" temploid="64D93A3C4C274e748E2A47F844AF6117" must="1" spec="id" dtref="_000001FECA5FA920">
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang="en-US">OBDMID</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang="en-US">The OBDMIDs $00, $20, $40, $60, $80, $A0, $C0, $E0 result in an response that contains the supported OBDMIDs in the respective range. (e.g. $40 -&gt; response describes the PIDs in range $41-$60.
Note, in this case one OBDMID is mandatory and at most 6 OBDMIDs are allowed.
Each other OBDMID results in a response that contains the corresponding OBDMID data (e.g. $03 -&gt; response contains info about Oxygen Sensor Monitor Bank1-Sensor3).
Note, in this case exactly 1 OBDMID is required/allowed.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>OBDMID</QUAL>
</STATICCOMP>
</REQ>
<POS oid="09A8A136A56F4a8293E126317B7642B9" temploid="5C73142DDC9549f38380A9D8199CB26B">
